ENTRY            22072   20211228   20220319   20220317       2306
SUBENT        22072001   20211228   20220319   20220317       2306
BIB                 13         46
TITLE      Structure of unbound states in 29Si from neutron
            resonance spectroscopy of 28Si+n
AUTHOR     (H.Weigmann, P.W.Martin, R.Koehler, I.van Parijs,
            F.Poortmans, J.A.Wartena)
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,36,585,1987)
           (C,88MITO,,707,1988)
INSTITUTE  (2ZZZGEL)
FACILITY   (LINAC,2ZZZGEL) Geel 150 MeV linac. Pulsed beam with
            repetition rate 800 Hz, and burst widths between 0.7
            and 5 ns.
INC-SOURCE Hg-cooled uranium target. unmoderated for transmission
            measurements and both unmoderated and moderated with
            two Be-canned water moderators for the capture
            measurements.
SAMPLE     Transmission measurements: The sample was metallic
            silicon of natural isotopic composition and had a
            thickness of 0.07356 atoms/b.
           Capture measurements: The samples were compressed
            discs of natural silicon, each 8 cm in diameter and
            of thicknesses 8 mm and 16 mm.
DETECTOR   (SCIN) For transmission measurements. The detectors
            were placed at 400 m flight path. The dimensions of
            the NE 110 scintillators were 15x15x2 cm3 and 5 cm
            diameter by 2.5 cm thick, respectively.
           (BGO) For capture measurements. Four 7.5 cm diameter
            by 7.5 cm thick BGO detectors were used. They were
            placed at a flight path of 130 m at angles of 39, 90,
            125, and 141 degrees with respect to the neutron beam.
METHOD     (TOF,TRN) Transmission and capture measurements.
ANALYSIS   (MLA) Multi-channel multi-level R-matrix analysis were
            performed for the transmission data, using the code
            MULTI.
           (AREA) The capture gamma yield data were analysed
            with the area analysis code TACASI.
MONITOR    (26-FE-56(N,G),,ARE) The well-known 1.15 keV resonance
            was used to determine the absolute capture yields.
CORRECTION The transmission data were corrected for instrumental
            dead time and for background.
           The capture data were corrected for scattered neutron
            background, Compton contribution from higher energy
            gamma rays, multiple scattering and self shielding.
HISTORY    (19871019C) N.O.
           (19890531U) IF. Reference added
           (19970111A) N.O. BIB section corrected. 010 added.
           (20160208A) On. 002-003 restored. Major rev.in 004-006.
           (20211228A) SD: Correction in Subent 008.
ENDBIB              46
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           49
ENDENTRY             1
